description:
Dereference an id from `search`. You get the reading in one line, then the signed body, the URL that serves those bytes, and metadata: cell, band, signing time and key. The id can be an `emem:fact:` citation, a bare fact_cid, or an `emem:cell:` handle for a full cell. The value is the exact decimal string that the responder signed, never a new format. A fact handle writes nothing. A cell handle, like `emem_recall`, MATERIALIZES a missing band on a cold cell: it fetches, signs and stores it. The flags follow that path: readOnlyHint false.

When to use: Call this on each result that you will cite, before you quote the number. Quote the one-line reading. The body lets a reader check it, and emem_echo_verify grades what you emit against it. When a body is too large, the answer says so and gives the URL that serves it complete.

Example arguments: {"id":"emem:fact:defi.zb493.xoso.zcb6a:cxjiu7l54ujzrpnekp24n4534yojpue4mprddbvevnqtti3lh5bq"}
